---
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import Code from '../components/Code.astro';
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Playground" description="Test the Vite plugin and browser panel together." activePath="/playground/">
    <article>
        <p class="kicker">Integration testing</p>
        <h1>Exercise the complete request path.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
            The playground is a small micro frontend under <code>apps/playground</code>. It mounts the proxy panel and
            provides repeatable GET and POST requests with visible response data and timing.
        </p>

        <h2>Start with local mocks</h2>
        <Code code="pnpm dev:playground" label="terminal" />
        <ol>
            <li>Open the floating proxy panel.</li>
            <li>Select a profile, order, or availability scenario.</li>
            <li>Run the corresponding request in the playground.</li>
            <li>Compare status, response body, duration, and current cookies.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2>Connect a development API</h2>
        <Code
            code="PLAYGROUND_API_TARGET=https://dev-api.example.com pnpm dev:playground"
            label="terminal"
        />
        <p>
            The playground adds a Vite proxy for <code>/api</code>. Turning off all mocks or only one endpoint forwards
            matching requests to <code>PLAYGROUND_API_TARGET</code>, while the remaining endpoints stay local.
        </p>
        <Callout title="Use a trusted target" tone="warning">
            <p>The development target receives the original request path, method, headers, and request body.</p>
        </Callout>

        <h2>Available requests</h2>
        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Endpoint</th><th>What it demonstrates</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>GET /api/playground/profile</code></td><td>Default file, explicit files, and endpoint bypass.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>POST /api/playground/orders</code></td><td>Method-specific fallback plus 201 and 422 scenarios.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>GET /api/playground/availability</code></td><td>Immediate and delayed responses.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </article>
</DocsLayout>
